        "answer": {
          "short": "In increasing order of $n$: $2.00,\\ 2.42,\\ 2.85,\\ 3.27,\\ 3.70,\\ 4.12$.",
          "worked": "Use the unrounded prices when taking logarithms.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\log_{10}P(0)&=\\log_{10}(100)=2.00\\\\\\log_{10}P(20)&=\\log_{10}\\bigl(100(1.05)^{20}\\bigr)\\approx2.42\\\\\\log_{10}P(40)&=\\log_{10}\\bigl(100(1.05)^{40}\\bigr)\\approx2.85\\\\\\log_{10}P(60)&=\\log_{10}\\bigl(100(1.05)^{60}\\bigr)\\approx3.27\\\\\\log_{10}P(80)&=\\log_{10}\\bigl(100(1.05)^{80}\\bigr)\\approx3.70\\\\\\log_{10}P(100)&=\\log_{10}\\bigl(100(1.05)^{100}\\bigr)\\approx4.12\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 0,
        "responseSpace": "scaffold"
      },
