      {
        "id": "p40-q4-e",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "Use the log laws to prove that $\\log_{10}P=2+n\\log_{10}(1.05)$, and hence explain the shape of the second graph.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\log_{10}P=2+n\\log_{10}(1.05)$.\n\nThe second graph is a straight line with gradient $\\log_{10}(1.05)$ and vertical intercept $2$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\log_{10}P&=\\log_{10}\\bigl(100(1.05)^n\\bigr)\\\\\\log_{10}P&=\\log_{10}100+\\log_{10}(1.05)^n\\\\\\log_{10}P&=2+n\\log_{10}(1.05)\\end{align*}$$\nThis has the form $y=mn+c$, where $y=\\log_{10}P$, $m=\\log_{10}(1.05)$ and $c=2$. Thus the second graph is a straight line with positive gradient and vertical intercept $2$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
